  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 112 PM CDT Tue May 26 2026\n\nProspects for rain, especially beneficial rain over 0.5\", are \nbleak looking through the remainder of the period and beyond. \nThis is only worsened by our dry air mass affecting the region, \nwhich will yield afternoon humidity below 30% of most \nafternoons in the week ahead. That said, this air mass will be \nquite comfortable for being outside, though warm in the \nafternoon, the overnight should cool to the 50s and lower 60s \nmost nights ahead this week. This is all due to a blocking \npattern that is only expected to strengthen with time.\n\nPersistent blocking pattern (Omega block) with an unseasonably \nstrong ridge (2.5 sigma or close to the Max percentile per \nNAEFS/ENS) near the US-Canada border to support a high confidence \ndry forecast. NBM output has now removed mentionable PoPs (>15%) \nfrom the entire period and WPC 7 day QPF has dropped to zero for the \nCWA. Ensemble 50th percentile Total QPF solutions also have come \ndown further and now all show less than 0.10\" QPF through June 4th! \nGiven the dry ground (less than 60% of normal rainfall in past 30 \ndays) this will likely contribute to drought conditions \ndeveloping/worsening over the next 2 weeks. Time to start watering \nyour May flowers.",
